{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Entries now get a `word_count` computed on every save and returned in the API entry object; the build and existing unit and integration tests pass, but I added no tests for the new behaviour.\n\n- **Storage**: a new migration adds a nullable `entries.word_count` column. It is written on all three paths that save content: entry creation, feed-refresh update, and the title/content edit.\n- **Existing entries**: not backfilled \u2014 they stay null until they are next saved.\n- **API**: `word_count` is a nullable integer on the entry model and on the Go client's `Entry`.\n- **Counting rule**: whitespace-separated words of the content after `sanitizer.StripTags`. Tags are removed without inserting a space, so `<p>a</p><p>b</p>` counts as one word; say if adjacent block elements should count separately.", "t": 1794462663.003}
